POC Scope and Success Criteria
The POC will implement a scaled-down version of our concrete exemplar (the Service Intake Request) in both platforms. To objectively determine the correct architectural fit for the Mosaic Interaction Hub, the evaluation will be strictly measured against the following servicing-domain requirements:

Latency & Execution Speed: The total round-trip time for a state transition must meet the real-time response requirements of an active, associate-facing UI.

Data Sovereignty (Store-by-Reference): The engine must successfully route the workflow using only abstract reference IDs, proving it can operate without ingesting or persisting any PII/PCI payload data.

Stateless Elasticity: The solution must demonstrate the ability to deploy and scale dynamically as stateless containers within our existing OpenShift infrastructure.

Infrastructure Alignment: The ease of versioning workflow models alongside core code and deploying them through our standard automated CI/CD pipelines.

Following the conclusion of this time-boxed POC, the engineering team will present the benchmarked metrics to the board to finalize the architectural decision.
